WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.460
The idea of free college got a lot of

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.230
attention during the 2016 election. Now,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.030
it sounds pretty progressive, but what

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.280
many people don't know is that students

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.750
from rich families are the ones who

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.880
stand to benefit the most. Consider what

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.529
happened when Oregon passed a free

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:21.750
community college program. The average

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.460
poor student got just six hundred

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.050
dollars out of the program, but the

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.699
average rich student got nearly

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.519
twenty-five hundred dollars. That's right -
 rich

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:31.590
students got four times as much money as

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.500
poor students out of free community college.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.080
Now, the reason for this is that we

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.649
already have lots of programs to help

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:39.480
lower-income students afford college.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.700
For instance, the Pell Grant program

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.100
gives students from poor families up to

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.050
fifty-eight hundred dollars to help them

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.090
pay for college. That's enough to pay

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.010
tuition and then some at many community

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.860
colleges. That means poor students pay

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.780
much less tuition than rich students,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.570
once you factor in financial aid. It's no

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.280
surprise that when you get rid of

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.199
tuition rich students are the big

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:03.449
winners. Don't you think we could spend

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:06.510
that money better somewhere else?

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.340
To learn more about my take on free college,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.110
check out the links in the description

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.420
below. Also, let us know what other topics

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.460
you want a AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

